"Build a feature that allows an RM (Relationship Manager) to call a customer through the Web using VoIP, then auto-summarize the call and fill the data into a form, and use AI to suggest a selling scenario. A FreeSWITCH server runs on EC2 with a working calling demo. MicroSIP installed on the RM machine (which opens the web) is invoked to call the customer; after the call, the recording file saved on the EC2 instance is downloaded, a speech-to-text API is called, and an LLM performs the smart tasks (summary, form fill, sales scenario suggestion). Currently only the calling-demo source code exists. What needs to be added: Figma design, database design, speech-to-text integration, backend source code (prefer Spring Boot), and UI implementation. This is a CRM-domain hackathon project."
